# Runtime

Follow [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md), the single source of repository instructions.

- Execution belongs in Rust. SDKs and bindings expose it; do not add a TypeScript fallback.
- Keep execution deterministic by default and all runs resumable.
- Checkpoint after every node completion and every state mutation.
- Emit one event per node lifecycle transition, in order. Preserve run lifecycle events.
- Human gates suspend with `run_suspended`; resume restores the latest checkpoint and avoids
  repeating completed side effects.
- Resolve named conditions through a registry/native callback seam; never evaluate graph strings.
- Keep node handlers, registries, checkpointer, and event delivery responsibilities distinct.
  Conditions are pure; I/O belongs at declared tool/storage/provider boundaries.
- Enforce node retry policies. Preserve all invariants across retries, failures, fan-out,
  cycles, subgraphs, streaming, interrupts, and cancellation.
- Cover these behaviors on the real Rust execution path. Runtime invariant changes require
  maintainer review and a public ADR before implementation.
